⍝ division is total:  x ÷ 0 = 0  (the 'meadow' convention), so every denominator that is ever built is non-zero and ≐ is an equivalence
÷ ξ η ≔ ((∅ᶻ (◀ η)) 0 (⊗ (⊠ᶻ (◀ ξ) (▶ η)) (⊠ᶻ (▶ ξ) (◀ η))))
≐ ∶ ℚ[i] → ℚ[i] → 𝔹
≐ ξ η ≔ (≡ (⊠ᶻ (◀ ξ) (▶ η)) (⊠ᶻ (◀ η) (▶ ξ)))
⍝ the sign of Re z, read off the digits in one pass (no search).  With blocks cⱼ as above, Re z = Σ rⱼ (−4)ʲ with rⱼ = Re cⱼ ∈ {−1 … 3};
⍝ the blocks below J add up to at most 4ᴶ − 1 in absolute value, so sign(Re z) = sign(r_J)·(−1)ᴶ for the highest J with r_J ≠ 0.
⍝ The automaton reads the blocks least significant first and remembers the sign the last non-zero block gives.
